1967,EQ ID 1967,Panfolder (WC#2043-M1),Fabrication,1002,"1.) Check the condition of the hydraulic fluid and change if necessary. Use HLP ISO 46 or equivalent.
2.) Change the hydraulic fluid filter. 
3.) Check electrical connections.",Pending,3/18/2023,,Technician,0.00,0.00,0.00,,,[]
1967,EQ ID 1967,Panfolder (WC#2043-M1),Fabrication,6081,"1.) Grease the top and bottom Z axis screw bearings.
2.) Check the Z axis guides. Clean and re-grease as needed.
3.) Grease the two A axis screw bearings.
4.) Check the A axis guides. Clean and re-grease as needed.
5.) Grease the X axis screw bearings. Wipe off excess dirt and grease from the guide rails.
6.) Drain condensation from the air filter.
7.) Check the hydraulic oil level.",Pending,6/23/2023,,Technician,0.00,0.00,0.00,,,[]
1967,EQ ID 1967,Panfolder (WC#2043-M1),Fabrication,1004,"1.) Grease the B axis. It is the large brass pin with the grease fitting in the end.
2.) Check the tension and condition of the X axis drive belt.
3.) Check the hydraulic line mounting.
4.) Clean the AC filter.",Pending,4/18/2022,,Technician,0.00,0.00,0.00,,,[]
