257,EQ ID 257,"Gauer Deburring Machine 40""",Fabrication,5895,"1.) Check the E-stop, switches, and electrical cables for wear, damage, and proper operation.
2.) Check for air leaks and oil leaks.
3.) Remove covers and blow the dust and debris out of the machine.  
4.) Check all chain and sprockets for wear/damage. 
5.) Make sure the all bolts are tight. . 
6.) Clean and lube the width adjustment screws.
7.) Clean all rollers. Use sandpaper or scotchbrite as needed
8.) Lightly lube all chains, sprockets, etc.",Pending,12/5/2023,,Technician,0.00,0.00,0.00,,,[]
